## Quick start

```bash
cp .env.example .env        # then edit it
make install                # pip install -e ".[dev]"
make dev                    # {{ stack.cmd.dev }}
make test                   # pytest
```

API docs: http://localhost:8000/docs

## Production (Docker + Postgres)

```bash
export SECRET_KEY=$(python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))")
make docker                 # runs migrations, then the server
```

The container runs as a non-root user and applies database migrations (`{{ stack.cmd.migrate }}`) on start.
After changing a model, create a migration with `make migration`.

